    "title": "When is Easter 2026? What Kansans should know about the holiday's date",
    "text": "March 27, 2026, 4:05 a.m. CTEaster is near, but you may be curious what day the holiday falls on this year because it never lands on the same date two years in a row.Here's everything you should know about this year's holiday.When is Easter 2026?Easter is always observed on a Sunday. In 2026, Easter Sunday falls on April 5.Is Easter early or late in 2026?This year, Easter isn't early or late. It can happen as early as March 22 or as late as April 25. The 2026 celebration falls almost in the middle of the range.Why Does Easter’s Date Change?Easter is known as a “movable feast,” meaning it does not fall on the same calendar date each year. Unlike Christmas, which is fixed to the solar calendar, Easter is determined by the Moon, said the Old Farmers Almanac.Easter Sunday is observed on the first Sunday after the Paschal Full Moon. The Paschal Full Moon is the Full Moon that occurs on or after the Church’s fixed date for the spring equinox, March 21.Why do people celebrate Easter?Christians believe that Jesus of Nazareth died by crucifixion on Good Friday. Easter is a Christian religious holiday that celebrates the resurrection of Jesus Christ three days after his death.What's the most common Easter Date?Over a 500-year period (from 1600 to 2099), Easter most often falls on March 31 or April 16, said the Old Farmer's Almanac.When is Good Friday this year?Good Friday marks the day Christians believe Jesus died on the cross. According to the Bible, he was sacrificed to pay for the sins of mankind and his body was later laid to rest in a nearby tomb. In 2026, Good Friday is April 3.Contributing: Josh Kelly, The Oklahoman & Bonnie Bolden, Clarion Ledger",
